.TH "tum\-popup" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-popup\f[R] \[em] open the interactive menu over every command
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum popup\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum popup\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
Open a \f[CR]display\-popup\f[R] menu that exposes every \f[CR]tum\f[R]
command through arrows and enter.
It is the catch\-all for anything without a dedicated key binding: the
popup delegates to the same CLI commands every binding uses, so anything
doable in the popup is scriptable and a CLI fix fixes the UI too.
.PP
Requires tmux ≥ 3.2 (the binding constraint is
\f[CR]display\-popup\f[R]).
If the popup is not implemented, the chooser and the cheatsheet still
cover discovery.
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum popup                # full interactive menu of every command
# bound to  t u  in the shipped tum\-bindings.conf
.EE
.SS SEE ALSO
\f[B]tum\-cheatsheet\f[R](1), \f[B]tum\-keymap\f[R](5),
